A||||8||JetroGT||Still re-working.||||1||
Z||000000||JetroGT||12-28-1999||05:04 AM||||<BR>Well, I finally got my oil sending unit replaced today. For a while I thought the needle was going to break off of the extra gauge pod. When I am stoped while in drive the pressure reads at about 20-25. And in drive it's about 45. With 126,000 miles on the car I think thats pretty good! The old one was giving me crazy readings of 80+ pounds of pressure, then at low speeds it would just peg.<BR> I was supposed to get my coolent flushed also but they found a hose that was leaking fluid on the right side of the radiator. My coolent is only good for -10F. And it's not getting any warmer out.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-28-1999||10:59 PM||||Especially not where you live.  Make sure you add the correct mixture.  100% antifreeze isn't any better than all water.  I think 50/50 is the correct mix, but I could be wrong.  (If I am wrong, please let me know in private.  That way I can find somebody to blame it on! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000002||olympic||12-28-1999||11:11 PM||||A 50/50 mix of antifreeze and water will give you -34C (-30F) protection, thats fine for most areas. Around here they suggest 60/40. Your right, you should never go stronger than 70/30.||||reg||1
