Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-30-1999||12:32 AM||||Steven--You know how to fix that, don't you?  Just don't stop at the redlights! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||7
Z||000007||Steven||12-30-1999||11:15 AM||||You say that as a joke, but about a month ago I hurt my left foot and could not push the clutch in without extreme pain. So to keep myself from hurting I would push in the clutch with my right foot, shift, and release. Then hit the gas. This trick only worked on 2nd, 3rd, and 4th gear shifts. Frist gear had to use both feet. So I tried to time the lights just right, and the only time I had to come to a complete stop was in my driveway. It was the only time that I did not like my car.  <p>[This message has been edited by Steven (edited 12-30-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||12-30-1999||07:57 PM||||Timing the lights is a trick used by most truck drivers since it takes a lot to stop and start.  I drove through Miami once (not during rush hour!) without stopping.  Never picked my left foot up off the floor.  (Of course, you don't have to use a clutch to shift gears in a big truck--it's called "floating the gears")||||reg||1
